---
layout: changelog
title: "Introducing MCP Events"
date: 2026-10-19
cover: /images/blog/announcing-mcp-events/cover.avif
tags: mcp
---

Agents connected to the [Appwrite MCP server](/docs/tooling/ai/mcp-servers) can now subscribe to events in your project and react when they happen, without polling. Six events are available at launch: new users, failed function executions, finished function and site deployments, new rows, and uploaded files.

Agents on your machine receive events over an open stream, and agents with a public HTTPS endpoint receive them as signed webhook calls. Each subscription is an Appwrite webhook in your project. [Pi](https://pi.dev) supports MCP Events through the [`pi-mcp-events`](https://github.com/mikekelly/pi-mcp-events) extension.

